    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307-a1">

                <pb facs="0610" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg514"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Board of Trade</hi>, (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Harbor
                                Department</hi>,)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Whitehall
                            Gardens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-05-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28,
                    1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From the London Gazette of May 29, 1874.]</p>
                <p>The board of trade have received through the secretary of state for the colonies
                    a dispatch from the officer administering the government of the Gold Coast,
                    inclosing an official notice announcing that the blockade of the Gold Coast,
                    established December 15, 1873, was raised on the 17th of April, 1874.</p>
            </div>
